.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH ckman-piv-sign 1  ckman 
.SH NAME
ckman\-piv\-sign \- Sign data with a slot\*(Aqs key (hash with \-\-hash, or pass the exact operation input with \-\-raw)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBckman\-piv\-sign\fR [\fB\-\-hash\fR] [\fB\-\-raw\fR] [\fB\-P\fR|\fB\-\-pin\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fISLOT\fR> <\fIINPUT\fR> <\fIOUTPUT\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Sign data with a slot\*(Aqs key (hash with \-\-hash, or pass the exact operation input with \-\-raw)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-hash\fR \fI<HASH>\fR
Hash algorithm for the message (RSA/ECC; default SHA\-256). SM2, Ed25519 and ML\-DSA\-65 sign the message directly
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
sha256
.IP \(bu 2
sha384
.IP \(bu 2
sha512
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-raw\fR
Input is already the exact operation input: a modulus\-sized encoded block (RSA), a digest (ECC/SM2), or the message (Ed25519)
.TP
\fB\-P\fR, \fB\-\-pin\fR \fI<PIN>\fR
PIN code (prompted when needed)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fISLOT\fR>
PIV slot
.TP
<\fIINPUT\fR>
File containing the message (or, with \-\-raw, the exact operation input) (\*(Aq\-\*(Aq for stdin)
.TP
<\fIOUTPUT\fR>
File to write the signature to (\*(Aq\-\*(Aq for stdout). ECDSA signatures are DER\-encoded; RSA/Ed25519 are raw bytes
